  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EVALUATION OF THE REPRODUCTIVE BIOLOGY OF THE KEMP S RIDLEY SEA TURTLE AT RANCHO NUEVO, MEXICO: IMPLICATIONS FOR SPECIES CONSERVATION AND RECOVERY</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to support the Mexico-US Binational Kemp&apos;s Ridley conservation project in Mexico. The intent of this project is to assess nesting beach management practices, nesting female reproductive output, and predator threats to nests, to inform and improve management practices, and enhance population recovery. Activities include: (1) assessing sex ratios in hatchery and in situ nests; and (2) assessing hatching fitness from hatchery and in situ nests; (3) assessing arribada size ; and (4) assessing predator threats to in situ nests.</narrative>
  </description>
